      "math_academy_id": "q-213251",
      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "Consider the following relation defined on the set $A=\\{5,8,10\\}.$ \n\n$$\nR=\\{(5,5),(5,8),(8,10),(10,5),(10,8)\\}\n$$\n\nSelect the options that make the following reasoning correct:\n\nSince \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}, \n\nthe relation is \n{{field-3}}.",
      "worked_solution": "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nIn our case, the relation is defined on $\\{5,8,10\\},$ and we have\n\n$$\n(5,5)\\in R,\\,(8,8)\\notin R,\\,(10,10)\\notin R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can conclude the following:\n\n$\\,$ Since $(8,8)\\notin R$ $\\text{and }(5,5)\\in R,$ the relation is $\\text{neither reflexive nor irreflexive}.$",
